# Go
/heliograph
/heliograph-relay
*.exe
*.test
/vendor/

# site
/site/node_modules/
/site/dist/
/site/.astro/

# Release artefacts, built by CI and by packaging/mcpb/build.sh
/dist/

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Local agent tooling state
.serena/
.superpowers/

# local
.env
*.local

# never
*.key
*.pem
.git-token

# Kept although the station has no Python: a contributor's editor or a stray
# tool can still drop these, and they should never reach a commit.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# Captured runs belong in a transport repo, never in this one. The station's
# own ignore file ships as station/bash/gitignore and deliberately does NOT
# ignore these - there, committing a log is the entire point. Here, a log is
# a real investigation that has escaped into a public repo.
**/ops-logs/*.txt
# Station state, dropped into station/bash/ by running the suite locally. The
# station's own ignore file covers these in a TRANSPORT repo; this one has to
# cover them here, or a local test run leaves them staged. Both spellings: a
# checkout predating the rename still writes the .agent-* names.
.agent.lock
.agent-state
.agent-approved
.station.lock
.station-state
.station-approved
.station-delivery
.station-relay-state
.station-tp-init
.station-service.log

# Terraform local state and provider cache. State for the templates under
# station/bash/azure/*/ is never meant to be shared through this repo - each
# deployer runs their own apply against their own estate - and a .tfstate
# file can carry resource IDs and, depending on the resource, attribute
# values that belong in nobody's git history. .terraform.lock.hcl is NOT
# listed here: that one is meant to be committed, so every apply resolves
# the same provider version.
**/.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
